meta {
  name: 14e Open the Schreiben block
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/exams/attempts/{{b2AttemptId}}/blocks/SCHREIBEN/start
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() >= 400) {
    throw new Error(
      "HTTP " + res.getStatus() + ": " + JSON.stringify(res.body) +
        (res.getStatus() === 401 ? "  (re-run Student Activation / 00 Login student)" : "")
    );
  }
}
docs {
  BLOCKS RUN IN ORDER. Schreiben is position 3, so this is
  BLOCK_OUT_OF_ORDER until LESEN_SPRACHBAUSTEINE (1) and HOEREN (2) have
  each been started AND submitted — exam-sitting.service.ts refuses any
  block with an unfinished earlier one, because telc sits them in sequence
  and a candidate cannot skip ahead.

  So before this request, for each of LESEN_SPRACHBAUSTEINE and HOEREN:

    POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exams/attempts/{{b2AttemptId}}/blocks/<BLOCK>/start
    POST {{baseUrl}}/api/exams/attempts/{{b2AttemptId}}/blocks/<BLOCK>/submit

  Empty answers are fine — they score zero, which is what a candidate who
  ran out of time gets, and the point here is reaching Schreiben.

  Worth watching on the HOEREN start: its deadline comes back 20 minutes
  out, not 30. That is this phase's one changed number arriving where a
  candidate actually meets it, read from exam_block_durations by the
  sitting's level.
}
